      "slug": "gram:n3-sono-kekka",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Invariable sentence-initial connective. The record's own formation is [situation 1]。その結果、[outcome], placing その結果 at the HEAD of the second clause; the その points back at the whole preceding sentence rather than attaching to any word in it, and nothing is inflected. The closed op enum has no prepend operation, so any step list would either emit the bare clause or falsely license appending その結果 after it.",
      "nuance_tags": ["cause"],
      "usage_contexts": ["written", "academic", "business"]
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-sono-tame-ni",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Invariable sentence-initial connective used between two independent clauses ([goal]。そのために、[action]). The record explicitly separates it from the 〜ために that DOES attach to a verb (合格するために) and keeps そのために outside any single clause, so there is no base to transform; the closed op enum has no prepend operation either.",
      "nuance_tags": ["intention"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-sono-ue",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Invariable sentence-initial connective. The record states outright that it comes after a complete clause and introduces the next one ([Clause A]。その上、[Clause B]) and that it requires no special form of the verb or adjective preceding it — the record itself asserts there is no derivation. The closed op enum has no prepend operation, so nothing can be emitted without inverting the rule.",
      "nuance_tags": ["emphasis"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-sore-to",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Invariable connective placed at the HEAD of the second clause (Item 1 + それと + Item 2, それと、…). Nothing is inflected, and それ+と is a frozen unit here rather than a productive attachment of the particle と to a base. The closed op enum has no prepend operation, so a step list would have to append it and would license *買い物それと.",
      "nuance_tags": [],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "casual-friends"]
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-sore-tomo",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Invariable connective standing BETWEEN two interrogative clauses (Question 1？ それとも Question 2？). Both clauses stay in plain form and neither is transformed by それとも, and the closed op enum has no prepend operation, so no ordered build over a single base can place it.",
      "nuance_tags": [],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-sukoshimo-nai",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Circumfix built on a pre-predicate adverb. The record is precise (すこしも sits before the term to be negated and the predicate must go negative: verb 〜ない/〜ません, i-adjective 〜くない, na-adjective/noun 〜ではない), but the closed op set has only append and no prepend, so the すこしも slot cannot be produced by an ordered build. Steps covering only the negative half would emit 書かない as if it were the pattern, and the negation cannot be dropped either: the record states すこしも never appears with an affirmative predicate.",
      "nuance_tags": ["emphasis"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
